# @datadack packages are served by GitHub Packages, which requires auth even for
# reads, so the token lives here rather than being threaded through the build.
#
# Must be a classic PAT with only read:packages — npm.pkg.github.com does not
# accept fine-grained tokens. read:packages is not per-package, so the way to
# limit it is on the package: give a dedicated machine account Read on
# @datadack/serverless-ui only, and use that account's token here.
#
# The trailing slash on the registry URL is required. bun matches the auth line's
# key (//npm.pkg.github.com/) against the registry URL; without the slash the
# match fails, no Authorization header is sent, and the registry answers 401 with
# nothing naming the cause.
#
# It is committed, so treat it as readable by anyone with access to this repo and
# rotate it here when needed. It does not reach the shipped image: the Docker
# runtime stage copies only web/dist out of the frontend stage.
@datadack:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com/
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=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
